    "text": "Skip to content\n7. Hinges of certainty\n\nDoubt it \u00b7 On Certainty\n\n1\nDoubt it\nThe river-bed\n\nCheck a claim. Each check takes some things for granted while it runs. Check one of those too, and see what that check takes for granted. Then try doubting everything at once.\n\nTO CHECK\n\nThe bakery opens at eight on Saturdays.\n\nRead the sign on the bakery door.\nPhone the bakery and ask.\nAsk a neighbour who shops there.\n\nThe idea\nOn Certainty \u00a7341\n\n\u201c\u2026the questions that we raise and our doubts depend on the fact that some propositions are exempt from doubt, are as it were like hinges on which those turn.\u201d\nRead the whole passage\nAbout this game\nHow to play\nEach session starts with something to do: check a claim and then what the check takes for granted, or sort claims into the water and the river-bed for two different years.\nThen answer questions about what you saw. A wrong answer gets a reply explaining why; try again.\nEach round ends with the point it shows, and each session with the passage it comes from.\nThe idea\n\nDoubting needs something it does not doubt, as a door needs hinges that stay put.\n\nOn Certainty \u00a7341. Read the passage",
